sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Positives: the seven record/code disagreements of Pass 3.1 are gone - criteria doc L62 / L64, YAML L112, KG verified_laws L513, script header L12 / L25 / L31-L34 and the Law 6 docstring L469-L477 all state what the code computes (+10 restored); the math-KG YAML loci were shifted with the code (L28 L177-L233, L45 L239-L285, L60 L291-L339, L76 L345-L412, L95 L418-L457, L114 L463-L548, L131 L418-L457, L150 L554-L588; each starts at its `def`; `verify_integrity.py --loop-yaml` 0 violations); the uncommitted MathOfBiology.lean duplicate is gone (+2); the summary JSON records git_commit and script_sha256 and the hash equals the committed script (+1); C4 only on Laws 4 and 8, C2 withdrawn from 5 and 7, O/T counts agree across script, YAML, docs and KG; both Lean checks pass. Deductions: docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json was hand-edited, not regenerated - its 8 code_locus values (L347, L381, L415, L448, L482, L515, L548, L580) are the pre-commit numbers, so Laws 2-8 point 8 lines early and no longer start at their `def` (-3); its domain_summary names (L1068 Stoica, L1139 Morozov) contradict its verified_laws names and the script (-1); Lean comments / theorem name and script comments L552 / L683 keep the dropped attributions (-1); `verified_measurements` is still the referee's Pass 3 sidecar (22 stale entries, L627 citing a non-existent MathOfBiology section) with two entries rewritten by the builder under the referee's meas_ids, and no generator script exists (-8); C3 for Laws 4, 5, 7 rests on the soft 'in the primary source' clause with a single implemented_by each (-3); the Lean classifiers are regex-based and would still accept a conclusion that mentions a bound name trivially (-2); README L4 and KG L627 cite a MathOfBiology section that no longer exists (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L1068–L1068: domain_summary name 'Bongard-Levin Polycomputing & Stoica Multi-Observer Commutative Readout Law' (and L1139 'Shreesha-Morozov-Levin ...'): the script (L779, L821), docs (L63, L66), YAML (L77, L132) and the payload's own verified_laws dropped these names in Pass 3.2; the file contradicts itself again <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json#L1068-L1068>",
            "docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L347–L580: verified_laws code_locus values: L177-L225, L231-L277, L283-L331, L337-L404, L410-L449, L455-L540, L410-L449, L546-L580 - the Pass 3.1 (918-line) numbers. In the committed 941-line script the defs are at L177/239/291/345/418/463/418/554; e.g. L231 is inside Law 1's return dict and L455 is inside Law 5/7's. The payload was not regenerated when the YAML was; Pass 3.1 R8 regresses for this artefact <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json#L347-L580>",
            "docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L602–L631: m1 method 'Line-by-line classification of the 918-line script ... (L177-L225) ... (L231-L277)' and m2 method 'MathOfBiology.lean L1200-L1375 (identical text ...)': stale with respect to the 941-line script and the 956-line MathOfBiology.lean of this commit. No script generates the payload <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json#L602-L631>",
            "docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L647–L675: m4 value_raw '17', unit 'entries_of_18', method 'api.crossref.org ... 17/17 DOIs resolve with exact title and author list of record' and m5 value_raw '0', method 'All 7 Pass 3.1 discrepancies reconciled in Pass 3.2 ...' under meas_ids 2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit-v3-...-m4 / -m5. These are the referee's identifiers; the referee's sidecar read 13 and 7 when this commit was made. Builder-authored measurement values under referee attribution, in the artefact that feeds the KG and nanopubs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json#L647-L675>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L768–L769: Law 4 criteria_passed C1, C2, C3, C4 with implemented_by = this script only: C3 ('>= 2 implementations or cross-substrate validation in the primary source') rests on the soft clause; same for Laws 5 and 7 (single implemented_by) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L768-L769>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-8> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-1> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/math_kg_loops/levin-youtube-channel-math.yaml L12–L28" ;
        dct:description "Law 1: lean_locus L30-L60 (decl at L30, theorem L41), code_locus L177-L233 (def at L177, return closes at L233). Same pattern verified for all 8 laws at 9987ff10: lean loci start at L30/71/107/137/168/196/235/262, code loci at L177/239/291/345/418/463/418/554 (= def lines). `verify_integrity.py --loop-yaml` 0 violations (reproduced)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/math_kg_loops/levin-youtube-channel-math.yaml#L12-L28> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-2> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/verify_integrity.py L197–L254" ;
        dct:description "check_math_kg_loop_yaml: parses '#Ls-Le', checks existence and 1 <= s <= e <= len(lines), requires lean_decl and lean_theorem short names inside the lean slice and a `def ` inside the code slice, and classifies lean_code. Unchanged since Pass 3.1 (1fd1165f...)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/verify_integrity.py#L197-L254> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-3> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/verify_integrity.py L170–L187" ;
        dct:description "classify_lean_theorem_signature: splits at the depth-0 colon, collects bound names from `(x y : T)` groups and returns 'structural' only if one appears in the conclusion (or the conclusion has ∀)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/verify_integrity.py#L170-L187> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-4> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L142–L153" ;
        dct:description "Suite classifier applies the same rule (bound name must appear in the conclusion); 8/8 structural, kernel exit 0 (reproduced). all_lean4_verified (L878) is derived from these, not a literal" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L142-L153> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-5> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json L1–L3" ;
        dct:description "git_commit '7595b0cd' and script_sha256 38fcb818... recorded (new in Pass 3.2). The hash equals the committed script at 9987ff10; the commit is the parent, whose tree holds the older script - an unavoidable one-step lag the file does not explain" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json#L1-L3> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-6> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md L58–L66" ;
        dct:description "Law table: C4 only on Laws 4 and 8; C2 absent from Laws 5 and 7; O1 5 / O2 3 / T1 2 / T2 3 / T4 3 agree with script L716-L832, the YAML and the KG payload (checked); L62 +0.1866, L64 0.0015 -> 1.0000, L66 'first square strict dominance k = 25' match the code" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md#L58-L66> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-7> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md L33–L33" ;
        dct:description "C4 rule now cites 'alpha_bias -> 0.90' as the regime-crossing example, matching L398 of the script" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md#L33-L33> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-code-traceability-8> a pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean L20–L290" ;
        dct:description "The 8 Levin theorems; compiles, 0 sorry (reproduced, lean 4.35.0); file unchanged since Pass 3 (88efd6ab...)" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L20-L290> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic; independent cross-provider MorphoEval referee, Pass 3 / 3.1 / 3.2)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

